# ✅ **Simple C Program for Matrix Multiplication**

**This code multiplies two matrices A and B and prints the result.**

### 👉 Works for any size (user inputs rows & columns)

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int r1, c1, r2, c2;
    int A[10][10], B[10][10], C[10][10];

    // Input sizes
    printf("Enter rows and columns of Matrix A: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &r1, &c1);

    printf("Enter rows and columns of Matrix B: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &r2, &c2);

    // Check valid multiplication
    if (c1 != r2) {
        printf("Matrix multiplication NOT possible.\n");
        return 0;
    }

    // Input Matrix A
    printf("\nEnter elements of Matrix A:\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < r1; i++)
        for (int j = 0; j < c1; j++)
            scanf("%d", &A[i][j]);

    // Input Matrix B
    printf("\nEnter elements of Matrix B:\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < r2; i++)
        for (int j = 0; j < c2; j++)
            scanf("%d", &B[i][j]);

    // Multiply
    for (int i = 0; i < r1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < c2; j++) {
            C[i][j] = 0;
            for (int k = 0; k < c1; k++)
                C[i][j] += A[i][k] * B[k][j];
        }
    }

    // Output
    printf("\nResult Matrix:\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < r1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < c2; j++)
            printf("%d ", C[i][j]);
        printf("\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

---

# ✔️ **How it works (super simple)**

### 1️⃣ Multiply row of A with column of B  
### 2️⃣ Add all products  
### 3️⃣ Store in result matrix C  

Example:  
C[i][j] = A[i][0]\*B[0][j] + A[i][1]\*B[1][j] + …  

